# PONS $101 — DEPLOYMENT, DEVOPS & REPRODUCIBILITY

PONS $101 is intended to be deployable as a working research system, not merely preserved as documentation.

This section defines the operational architecture required to run:

• the ROB indexer
• the research API
• the experiment registry
• the preflight engine
• the unsigned payload builder
• the agent runtime
• the research database
• the Discord integration
• the provenance exporter
• dashboards
• scheduled jobs
• GitHub Actions
• reproducibility releases

The operating objective is:

ONE REPOSITORY

MULTIPLE SERVICES

SEPARATE PERMISSIONS

REPRODUCIBLE DEPLOYMENT

HUMAN-CONTROLLED MAINNET AUTHORITY

==================================================
DEPLOYMENT PRINCIPLE
==================================================

Every component should be replaceable without destroying the canonical research record.

The architecture should prefer:

OPEN INTERFACES

VERSIONED CONFIGURATION

PORTABLE DATA

PUBLIC CHAIN EVIDENCE

DETERMINISTIC HASHES

REPRODUCIBLE BUILDS

over dependence on a single hosted provider.

PONS $101 should be capable of moving between:

local development

cloud infrastructure

self-hosted infrastructure

research servers

and

future decentralized infrastructure

without redesigning the entire research model.

