==================================================
PONS API
==================================================

pons-api provides normalized research access.

Responsibilities:

• experiment retrieval
• launch retrieval
• telemetry retrieval
• fee summaries
• wallet-pattern research
• preflight requests
• unsigned payload generation
• health information
• research export metadata

The API does not hold a production signing key.

==================================================
ROB INDEXER
==================================================

rob-indexer connects to public blockchain RPC infrastructure.

Responsibilities:

• monitor launch events
• discover token and curve relationships
• index buy events
• index sell events
• preserve raw logs
• normalize decoded logs
• calculate block-relative timing
• detect reorgs
• resume from checkpoints
• emit research observations

ROB should be restartable without losing its canonical position.

==================================================
INDEXER CHECKPOINT
==================================================

Persist:

chain_id

last_scanned_block

last_confirmed_block

last_scanned_block_hash

updated_at

software_version

On restart:

1. Read checkpoint.

2. Verify stored block hash remains canonical.

3. If canonical:

resume.

4. If not canonical:

enter REORG recovery.

